# Atrium — THE FINAL BLITZ: done

Completion date: 2026-09-15 (window 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-15; agent
session ran inside the blitz window ending 2026-09-20).
Commit range: d125eb7 (first docs commit) .. c062f13 (last roadmap
tick). Releases: v0.74.1, v0.75.0, v0.76.0 (all pushed, CI green,
verbatim annotated tags; v0.74.1/v0.75.0 Releases hand-created per
the then-current recipe, v0.76.0 auto-created by the new release.yml,
which is itself part of the release).

## What shipped

- v0.74.1: the VERSION file the v0.74.0 stamp emptied is restored
  (forward-only bump) and the sync is guarded in three layers
  (regression.sh step 0, CI guard, atrium-cli version-sync test).
- v0.75.0: the final-audit fix wave — fixture generation routed
  through the single-writer worker, the vault ledger seed moved off
  the GTK main thread, GUI imports and the weekly VACUUM off the
  main thread, undo rollback failures logged, the `:ID:`-less
  project duplication guard (mutation-checked test), CLI weekday
  date parsing, is:archived/is:queued reserved in spec 4.3.7, and
  the docs-accuracy clusters (schema, gtd-patterns, keymap, spec
  3.4/6/9/10, USAGE completion, the Ndaysout phantom, the
  scheduled_warning doc-comment).
- v0.76.0: the answered-gates stamp — board card-count memory guard
  (2,000+ cards toast), release.yml (tag checks + verbatim
  auto-Release), the v* protection ruleset (ruleset 23387454),
  mdBook published to Pages (virinvictus.github.io/Atrium/),
  SHA-pinned actions + fedora:44 + workflow hardening, Dependabot
  (github-actions only), and the perf re-baseline with the new
  scripts/gui_memory_probe.sh.
- Docs lanes: stamp-fatigue collapse of the three accreted headers,
  the full em-dash recast of every living prose file (~450 lines),
  the slop smalls, the Phase 24 alias record, backup-format notes,
  feature Slot 1-9 backlog boxes, and the post-1.0 splits boxes.

## Gate decisions (all recorded in roadmap.md, answered via prompts)

- Push: standing blitz grant (answered).
- v0.74.0 pushed tag: kept as-is (recommendation in force after the
  first ask went unanswered; v0.73.0 precedent).
- is:archived/is:queued: reserved (recommendation in force after the
  first ask went unanswered).
- Toolchain: keep tracking stable as the early-warning tripwire
  (recommendation in force; actions SHA-pinned regardless).
- Memory gate: keep budgets, guard the board, virtualisation is the
  fix path (answered).
- Tag CI + auto-Release, v* ruleset, Pages publish: all yes
  (answered).
- GitHub extras: Dependabot yes; secret scanning + push protection,
  SECURITY.md, issue templates, old-tag Releases all declined
  (answered).
- worker.rs / cli-main.rs splits: post-1.0 (answered).

